Falsifies `system_tests::user::tests::the_hardware_says_el0_cannot_read_the_kernels_memory`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect is the kernel's own **text** mapped EL0-readable, which is the one section the
sibling falsification of `a_user_program_cannot_read_a_kernel_address` does not reach: that
one maps `.rodata` user-readable and this test asks about `0xffff_0000_4008_0000`, the
kernel's text.

It is one bit on the constructor rather than one flag at the call site, because there is no
constructor for "kernel-executable and user-readable" and there should not be: `Flags` is a
capability word with a fixed vocabulary, and the honest way to write this defect is to widen
the vocabulary rather than to pick a wrong word out of it. `CAP_KERNEL_EXEC` is kept, so the
kernel still executes its own text; `CAP_USER` is added, so the leaf encoder writes
`AP_RO_EL0` and EL0 may read it. `UXN` stays set, because `CAP_USER_EXEC` is not added, so
the page is still not executable at EL0.

Expected to fail: `assert!(!mmu::user_can_read(KERNEL_TEXT), "the hardware says EL0 could
read the kernel's own text")`. That assertion is the one the test is named for and it is
answered by the silicon (`AT S1E0R`), not by a software walk, which is what makes this
record worth more than its sibling's: the fault counter in the other test is the kernel's own
bookkeeping, and this is the CPU.

**The precondition above it stays green**, which is the shape to check for. The test first
requires `mmu::translate(KERNEL_TEXT).is_some()`, and it still is: the page is mapped, it is
readable, and only the privilege level changed.

**Two host tests in `crates/paging` break under this patch and neither runs here.**
`Flags::kernel_code().bits()` is asserted against a literal in that crate's own unit tests,
and `paging`'s Kani harnesses reason about the encoder rather than the constructor. A full
`script/test` would catch the first. This sweep boots one kernel test and does not, which is
the honest scope of a kernel-test falsification and is stated in script/falsifications' BUGS.

diff --git a/crates/paging/src/flags.rs b/crates/paging/src/flags.rs
index 03860e171..fa453076e 100644
--- a/crates/paging/src/flags.rs
+++ b/crates/paging/src/flags.rs
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@ pub struct Flags(u64);
 impl Flags {
     /// Kernel code: readable and executable by the kernel, never writable, never user.
     pub const fn kernel_code() -> Self {
-        Flags(ACCESS_KERNEL_EXEC | ACCESS_GLOBAL)
+        Flags(ACCESS_KERNEL_EXEC | ACCESS_GLOBAL | ACCESS_USER)
     }
 
     /// Kernel constants: readable by the kernel, never writable, never executable by anyone.
